                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e3a58284-062c-3360-b620-0ed30fb32a54",
                                        "entry_id": "a288b448-4b74-305a-bad5-4db0a325f77d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ring of fractions of a given ring, such that the complement of the set of allowed denominators is an ideal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa49b1f9-1a07-4b5a-9f8b-1c077782ee81",
                                                "sense_id": "e3a58284-062c-3360-b620-0ed30fb32a54",
                                                "text": "3) Geometric interpretation of the localization.\n Let V be an irreducible algebraic variety. Then P = J(V) is a prime ideal of #92;mathbb#123;C#125;#91;X#95;1,...,X#95;n#93; and so #92;mathbb#123;C#125;#91;V#93;#61;#92;mathbb#123;C#125;#91;X#95;1,...,X#95;n#93;#47;J(V) is an integral domain.\n The localization #92;mathbb#123;C#125;#91;X#95;1,...,X#95;n#93;#95;P is a subring of #92;mathbb#123;C#125;(X#95;1,...,X#95;n) consisting of rational functions #92;#123;f#47;g#58;f,g#92;in#92;mathbb#123;C#125;#91;X#95;1,...,X#95;n#93;,g#92;notinP#92;#125; which are defined on a nonempty subset of V. If V = {x} is a point, then P is maximal and #92;mathbb#123;C#125;#91;X#95;1,...,X#95;n#93;#95;P#61;#92;#123;f#47;g#58;f,g#92;in#92;mathbb#123;C#125;#91;X#95;1,...,X#95;n#93;,g(x)#92;ne 0#92;#125; consists of rational functions which are defined at x."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
